  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) at 0.591 acc is the clear best so far, showing multiprofile aggregation adds ~10.6% over singleprofile (config_001). Image alone (config_010, 0.208) is very weak, so the RNA pipeline is the primary driver. Uncertainty: We don't yet know whether a more expressive aggregation (transformer) outperforms simple avgpool for combining multiple profiles. This experiment (config_003) is a clean single-variable test of aggregation method, changing only avgpool→transformer while holding everything else identical to config_002. It is the best next use of budget because: (1) it directly extends the strongest configuration, (2) it isolates one design decision so the result is interpretable, (3) the outcome informs every subsequent experiment—both RNA-only and multimodal—by telling us which aggregation to pair with other components, and (4) it avoids prematurely investing in multimodal fusion while the image modality's contribution remains unproven."
}

